WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
A real CT volume anchors the clinical state in image evidence.
The example uses de-identified arterial CT with 46 axial slices.

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
Parsing separates the liver and lesion into spatial objects.
These are matching dataset reference masks, replayed here.

00:16.000 --> 00:25.000
ClinicalCode binds measurements, units, time, and sources.
The lesion volume is 72.384 mL in the reference segmentation.

00:25.000 --> 00:34.000
The upper 3D view reconstructs the reference anatomy.
The lower view illustrates explicit state evolution over time.

00:34.000 --> 00:44.000
The volume and viability proxy follow a frozen rule contract.
This schematic rollout is not a learned patient forecast.

00:44.000 --> 00:48.000
Clinical observations become structured code,
then an explicit, inspectable state trajectory.
